VIKSIT BHARAT & THE FOREIGN POWERS: Reimagining India’s economic landscape and growth of strong foreign relations

BY:KEERTHI ARUNACHALAM

In foremost ,India's apparent transitions: fast - evolving economy,strong hold in 
democratic politics,with highest standard of military power,maritime security and 
enlarging technology advancement ,India is seen as a rising superpower with 
prominent regional dominion. 


The vision  of Viksit Bharat 2047 encompasses various aspects of 
development,including economic growth,social progress,environmental 
sustainability and good governance. Under the leadership of NDA led government 
since 2014 , here is the stats of  India’s dynamic and formidable stance on the world 
stage : World's 3rd largest military expenditure, 2nd largest armed force, 5th largest 
economy by GDP nominal rates and 3rd largest economy in terms of purchasing 
power parity.India’s foreign policy has witnessed a shift under the NDA leadership 
from ‘non - aligned’ foreign policy to display a heightened level of ‘assertiveness’ 
in its international engagements.According to a survey by Pew Research,A median of 46% 
say they have a favourable view of India, 
compared with a median of 34% with an unfavourable view. Substantial shares in 
some countries also do not share an opinion (16% median). Views of India are most 
positive in Israel, where 71% say they have a favourable view of the country.So we 
do see India’s strengthening its position in the world. 


The G20 also provided a platform for India  in the midst of conflicts and 
competition, development slowed down, hindering progress to a bright inclusive 
feature. Assuming the G20 Chair, “India sought to offer the world an alternative to 
status quo, a shift from a GDP-centric to human-centric progress”. India aimed to 
remind the world of inclusivity and thereby introduced the concept of Vasudhaiva 
Kutumbakam[One Earth,One Family and One Future].Also it is partnering with other 
developing countries to form strategic trade blocs in Asia like ASEAN,BRICS.


India with standards of living improving and robust supply of skilled 
workers,provides a thriving market for big tech giants to enter. E- commerce 
companies also have advantage of our humongous population which increase their 
markets and profits.Technology is being infused in various sectors like 
healthcare,education with government and private individuals partnering  and 
empowering citizens to become Digital India.Pandemic,geopolitical tensions,natural 
disasters,supply backlogs,strict measures imposed by dictatorial government, have 
driven many companies to shift from China and India is taking the advantage of 
being the next superpower with its adroit youth .With developing Infrastructure, 
innovation, and enabling policies and strategic schemes  further bolster the country's appeal, 
demanding finesse strategies for successful market entry and 
growth. 


According to Forbes India ‘United States of America,China ,Russia,Germany,United 
Kingdom’ are the top 5 superpowers in 2024.India is a growing superpower and 
position itself as a friendly partner , and tactfully negotiates diplomatically with its 
counterparts on controversial issues.It maintains its national interest and doesn’t 
let any country to dictate terms. 


The US - India is one of the most strategic relationships,which share values of 
commitment to democracy and upholding the  rules - based international system. 
Both share common interests in promoting global security,stability,and economic 
prosperity through trade,connectivity, and investment by signing various trade 
pacts and formation of a security strategic dialogue QUAD(comprising 
India,USA,Japan,Australia). 


The Russia - India relationship has remained stable since Russia has been a 
longstanding and time-tested partner of India and plays a key role in shaping India’s 
foreign policy.Both the countries consider their mutual affinity to be a ‘special and 
privileged partnership’. 


The relationship between India and Germany as Germany being the 5th biggest 
trade partner in the world.The countries are bonded traditionally strong by 
commercial,cultural and technological cooperation.India and Germany are the most 
important partners both bilaterally and in global context. 


The India-UK relationship is bound by strong ties of history and culture.India has 
always had  multifaceted bilateral relationship with UK.UK is India’s major trading 
partner. 


Other than 5 major superpowers, India , officially Republic of India,has fully 
diplomatic relations with 195 states.To make sure that India's opinions are heard on 
global platforms and that India is able to influence world opinion on issues of global 
dimensions, India is taking key steps in forming diplomatic ties with major 
economies,its neighbours  and also other developing countries .India’s foreign 
policy emphasises on mutual respect for sovereignty and territorial integrity, 
mutual non-aggression, non-interference in each other's internal affairs, equality 
and mutual benefit, and peaceful coexistence,At this time, Indian diplomacy finds 
itself at a pivotal moment. Owing to its coherent foreign policy and its willingness to 
occasionally flex its muscles beyond its immediate neighbourhood, India has 
captured the attention of great powers. 
